+The \texttt{torchANN} keyword defines a scalar component based on an artificial neural network (ANN) model previously trained using PyTorch. Similarly to the \texttt{linearCombination} and \texttt{neuralNetwork} components, the ANN model is expressed as a function of collective variable components. The model is loaded from a PyTorch-formatted file, defined by the keyword \texttt{modelFile}\cvgromacsonly{; the contents of this file are embedded in the TPR}.
 
